Share mapped member relations lazily

Carry monotone element maps through keys and child prefix trees so
member transport can share entire relation subtrees, including unchanged
columns between members. Compress contiguous IDs into offset runs.
Cache transformed children on demand so reads can borrow values without
rebuilding every prefix. Drop children without surviving rows.

Keep sparse updates map-driven and avoid preparing large image maps for
small source slices. General and temporarily non-functional maps retain
all images through an eager fallback. Mutations and canonicalization
materialize affected levels while preserving existing snapshots.

Compare both key and value mapping identities before skipping shared
differences. Account for deferred transformations and filtered suffixes
in finite-fuel traversal without forcing them before charging the work.

Validation: runtime, evaluator, and compile suites pass. Focused tests
cover selective reads, composition, equality, partial maps, sparse
updates, randomized set operations, and finite fuel. Generated member
mapping cases pass in native and desugared modes under both evaluation
strategies. Formatting and patch checks pass.
